bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_block_use_same_name_class_segv_2026-11-27, 0, "Registered 2026-11-27 by p3sweep4 wave-9 lane as the JIT-lane residual of interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27: block-scoped use of two lazily loaded same-named classes segfaults (exit 139) on the JIT lane; the interpreter lane resolves correctly after the parent fix. Root-cause direction: block-use arms bind the constructor into the local env + flat MODULE_GLOBALS but record no owner binding, so HIR lowering sees two colliding bare-name classes; fix direction is record_owner_binding in the block-use arms (as evaluation_helpers.rs:72 does for module-scope uses) plus a hir/lower investigation of the crash site. The document remains the authority for diagnosis and acceptance."
    jit_block_use_same_name_class_segv_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-28 p3sweep8: row re-closed - the wave-13 fix (PR #12398) is merged and verified; a merge had reverted this shard row to open while leaving the fix in source. Fix recap: the block-scope use lane loads only class TYPES (hir/lower stmt_lowering.rs:1795), MIR calls Pure(Thing.create), compile_call declares the sanitized import Thing_dot_create, and the pre-finalize NULL-jump guard compared raw MIR names so the call jumped to a NULL GOT slot (exit 139, even for a single block-used class); the guard now records the _dot_ spelling and demotes fail-closed; probes rc 0 with correct owner-discriminating output on all variants. Spec same_name_class_block_scoped_import_jit_spec green. Residuals recorded: block-used class instance methods still fail closed (bodies never linked); true JIT-native block-used imports need the hir/lower path to bring functions + owner-qualified registration into the unit. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_block_scoped_import_jit_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/codegen/jit.rs"

